---
import Lockup from './Lockup.astro';
import { footerGroups } from '../lib/site-navigation';

const year = new Date().getUTCFullYear();
---

<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="footer-grid">
      <div class="footer-brand">
        <a class="brand-link" href="/"><Lockup /></a>
        {/*
          The footer carried "Opaque to the relay. Open to inspection." and,
          under it, "Brand language is provisional — taglines are proposed,
          pending sign-off." Both are gone, by founder decision on 2026-08-04,
          and the tagline itself is still undecided: `docs/decisions.md` §1
          stays open. Dropping the line is not approving or rejecting it.

          Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters. The note was
          internal process copy — our own review state, shipped to every
          visitor on every page of the site, answering a question no customer
          asked. And "Opaque" is an absolute the rest of this site spends its
          effort not making: the carrier panel on the landing page prints
          `senderUserId alice` in the clear, and the fixed relay formula is
          deliberately narrower — the relay never needs message plaintext or
          device private keys. A brand line that overstates against our own
          published evidence is the one kind of copy this project cannot
          afford, whoever signs it off.

          The design contract requires an annotation only from a surface that
          *uses* a tagline, so a footer without one owes nothing. `/product`
          still does — its h1 is the proposed Product hero string — and that
          page now carries the annotation itself, scoped to the one page that
          needs it. See `src/pages/product.astro`.
        */}
        <p>End-to-end encryption for TypeScript applications. AGPLv3, or a commercial license.</p>
      </div>
      {footerGroups.map((group) => (
        <div>
          <h2>{group.heading}</h2>
          <nav aria-label={group.heading}>
            {group.links.map((link) => <a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a>)}
          </nav>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="footer-legal">
      <nav aria-label="Legal">
        <a href="/legal">Legal</a>
        <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a>
        <a href="/legal/relay-terms">Relay terms</a>
      </nav>
      <p>© {year} OpenE2EE LLC and OpenE2EE contributors.</p>
      <p>
        An independent implementation of the published Signal Protocol specifications. Not
        affiliated with, endorsed by, or wire-compatible with Signal Messenger LLC or Signal
        Technology Foundation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
